emblazonry:
n. The act or art of an emblazoner; heraldic or ornamental
   decoration, as pictures or figures on shields, standards, etc.;
   emblazonment.

implementing:
v apply in a manner consistent with its purpose or design
v ensure observance of laws and rules; 
v pursue to a conclusion or bring to a successful issue

sideling:
adv. Sidelong; on the side; laterally; also, obliquely;
   askew.
a. Inclining to one side; directed toward one side; sloping;
   inclined; as, sideling ground.

unhoused:
a. Driven from a house; deprived of shelter.
a. Not provided with a house or shelter; houseless;
   homeless.
